StandardForm],"Print",ExpressionUUID -> "d8f8ce6e-67f0-4e6e-b62d-c3578ed0215e"],Cell[
BoxData[
InterpretationBox[RowBox[{"\"Reading: the aperture makes 'which observers see the four-fold \"","\[InvisibleSpace]","\"open' a computed set, not a metaphor. On Div12 - the minimal \"","\[InvisibleSpace]","\"kernel-bearing algebra, forced into the subobject lattice by any \"","\[InvisibleSpace]","\"ordinary kernel (ordinary_kernel_div12_embedding) - the answer is \"","\[InvisibleSpace]","\"maximally fragile: identity alone. On Div24 the invariant grades: \"","\[InvisibleSpace]","\"three observers, two of them genuinely coarse. Boolean and linear \"","\[InvisibleSpace]","\"worlds have empty apertures everywhere: no observer, at any \"","\[InvisibleSpace]","\"resolution, ever sees a four-fold there.\""}],
SequenceForm["Reading: the aperture makes 'which observers see the four-fold ","open' a computed set, not a metaphor. On Div12 - the minimal ",
"kernel-bearing algebra, forced into the subobject lattice by any ","ordinary kernel (ordinary_kernel_div12_embedding) - the answer is ",
"maximally fragile: identity alone. On Div24 the invariant grades: ","three observers, two of them genuinely coarse. Boolean and linear ",
